title: Agricultural Policy
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: agricultural_policy_timer += 5; month_actions += 1
view-if: psoe_in_government = 1 and agriculture_minister_party = "PSOE" and agricultural_policy_timer == 0
card-image: img/campesino_trabaja.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Agricultural Policy

Spain's countryside is an explosive powder keg. Millions of landless peasants (*jornaleros*) in Andalusia and Extremadura starve under semi-feudal conditions, while vast estates (*latifundios*) remain underutilized by absentee landlords who are unconcerned with productivity, focusing instead on collecting rents to emulate the old aristocracy.

The Republic promised land to those who work it but transforming this promise into reality requires monumental financial resources for reparatios, surveys and technical aid. If we move too slowly the countryside will burn under anarchist agitation; if we act too aggressively we will push the landowners and the army into open rebellion.

[? if land_reform_progress > 0: *Land Reform Progress:* [+ land_reform_progress +] / 10. ?]

[? if cnt_militancy > 3: *Agrarian Agitation:* Anarchist influence in the rural south is critically high! ?]

[? if sanjurjada_seen == 1 and sanjurjada_confiscations == 0: *Opportunity:* Landed aristocrats implicated in the Sanjurjada can now have their estates seized without compensation! ?]

- @ira_small
- @ira_large
